{
 "note": "End-to-end latency and the FDC leg, recomputed from chain timestamps for every live run in which an XRPL payment led to an execute on Coston2 -- nineteen, as of 2026-10-01: fourteen to 2026-09-30 (the last two the grant video's cash-out and vault deposit), and five on 2026-10-01 (two status-page checks, the docs' SDK quickstart and cash-out, and a fourth FSA import). Nothing here comes from a script's own clock: every figure is a difference between an XRPL ledger close time and Coston2 block timestamps. Each run's voting round is the Relay's getVotingRoundId at its request's timestamp, and matches the round the executor recorded where it recorded one.",
 "computedAt": "2026-10-01",
 "definitions": {
  "total": "XRPL payment's ledger close -> the execute's block timestamp",
  "closeToRequest": "XRPL ledger close -> the block of the earliest FdcHub AttestationRequest for that payment",
  "fdcLeg": "that request's block -> the block in which the Relay emitted ProtocolMessageRelayed for FDC (protocol 200) and that request's voting round: when the round's Merkle root, and so the proof, became final on Flare",
  "rootToExecute": "root published -> execute: the DA Layer serving the proof, plus the relayer fetching it and submitting",
  "fdcShare": "fdcLeg / total"
 },
